<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The ORDER FLOW nav icon (owner order 2026-11-04).

    The owner supplied the reference as a black line drawing: three rounded
    ledgers stacked, a printed row inside each, and arrows that move value
    between them, one leaving to the left at the top, one curving down the
    left edge, one leaving the middle to the right and one curving in from
    the right, and one leaving to the left at the bottom.

    Drawn here as vector strokes rather than a bitmap, for two reasons the
    rest of this nav row already keeps: the neighbours are tinted with the
    page colour through android:tint (a bitmap would need one file per
    state), and a stroke stays sharp at every density without a second
    asset. The geometry is the reference's own: three boxes, a dash in each,
    three straight arrows and two curved ones.

    It is a stroke drawing with no fill, so the 42dp slot's 8dp padding
    leaves the three rows readable and nothing clips at the plate's edge.
-->
